+# HANDBOOK.md
+
+Harness evolution for [HANDBOOK.md](https://github.com/surge-ai/handbook), a benchmark in which an OpenHands office assistant must find a company handbook in its workspace, read it, and apply its rules across mail, Slack, Jira, calendar and files. Tasks are scored by per-task rubrics with partial credit.
+
+The loop mirrors `terminal_bench_2/`: baseline → propose → validate → smoke → benchmark → frontier, with the same state files and proposer. What is specific to HANDBOOK.md:
+
+- **Candidates are agent harnesses.** `agents/<name>.py` defines `class AgentHarness(HandbookRunner)`. `handbook_runner.py` is the overridable form of the benchmark's in-container OpenHands runner (system prompt, LLM, condenser, extra in-episode tools, events, conversation, run loop, tool-call budget). `candidate_agent.py` is the Harbor agent that uploads the candidate and the base into each task container. The environment, MCP tools and worker model are fixed. The 200-call budget can be lowered, not raised.
+- **Objective = mean rubric score** over all trials. The strict pass rate is reported beside it.
+- **Train / holdout by sibling rule-variants.** The ten base handbooks each have two variants in `scripts/run_eval.sh`: search runs on `train` (one variant per base), `--full-eval` runs the frontier and the baseline on `holdout` (the siblings) at 3 trials (`logs/<run>/holdout.jsonl`), and `smoke` is one train task.
+- **Leak audits** keep the loop inside the benchmark's rules (the worker must read the handbook in-episode; the harness never carries or pre-digests it). A candidate is rejected when its strings or comments overlap any task's handbook, instruction or verifier text (8-word n-grams, names of a single handbook family) or name forbidden paths. A benchmark is voided when any trial's tool call touches `/tests`, `/initial_data`, `/logs` or a verifier file.
+- **Section declarations.** Every candidate declares `prompt_sections()` (and `feedback_sections()` for text injected at run time). Validation renders the prompt on a sample task and requires at least 3 verbatim spans covering at least 80% of it.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+1. A HANDBOOK.md checkout with its base image and Harbor venv, as in the benchmark README:
+
+   ```bash
+   git clone https://github.com/surge-ai/handbook && cd handbook
+   docker build -t handbook_base docker/
+   uv venv .venv --python 3.13
+   uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python harbor -e ./agent_harness
+   cp .env.example .env   # add the worker's API key, e.g. OPENROUTER_API_KEY
+   export HB_ROOT=$PWD
+   ```
+
+2. Claude Code (`claude` on `PATH`) for the proposer.
+3. This directory's environment: `uv sync`.
+4. For the leak audits and `--vitals`: [agent-vitals](https://github.com/zwycl/agent-vitals) in some Python environment, given to the loop as `VITALS_PYTHON`. Build the leak-audit corpus once, **outside this directory** (it holds every task's documents, and the proposer must never read it):
+
+   ```bash
+   $VITALS_PYTHON -m vitals.addons.metaharness.audit.handbook_leaks corpus \
+       --tasks $HB_ROOT/tasks --out ~/handbook-audit/corpus.jsonl
+   export HB_LEAK_CORPUS=~/handbook-audit/corpus.jsonl
+   ```
+
+   Without agent-vitals the leak audits are skipped; without a corpus the candidate code audit is skipped. The loop prints which audits are active at startup.
+
+## Quick Start
+
+Smoke-check the baseline on one task:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/run_eval.sh agents/baseline_openhands.py smoke 1 1
+```
+
+Run the loop:
+
+```bash
+uv run python meta_harness.py --run-name hb1 --iterations 5
+```
+
+Add `--full-eval` to finish with the holdout evaluation.
+
+## With agent-vitals read maps
+
+`--vitals` replays an outcome-stratified subsample of every benchmark's trials (`--vitals-subsample`, default 6) through a local BF16 copy of the worker (GPU) and writes a per-section read digest for the next proposer step:
+
+```bash
+VITALS_PYTHON=/path/to/agent-vitals-env/bin/python \
+VITALS_MH_REFERENCE_GGUF=/models/Qwen3.6-27B-BF16-00001-of-00002.gguf \
+uv run python meta_harness.py --run-name hb1v --iterations 5 --vitals
+```
+
+After each benchmark the loop calls `vitals metaharness replay-inloop-handbook` and then `vitals metaharness digest-handbook`. Both hooks are non-fatal. The proposer prompt then names:
+
+- `jobs/<run>/<job>/vitals_digest.md` (+ `.parquet`, `vitals_delta.parquet`) per benchmarked agent and `logs/<run>/reports/vitals_iteration_NN.md` per iteration
+- the raw store `logs/<run>/vitals/<agent>--handbook/store`, with the add-on's schema and standalone loader
+
+The rubric score stays the only objective. The proposer is told that read maps are evidence for a mechanism, must be corroborated by a transcript (trial and turn), and are never a target. Candidates may name their parent in `base_system`, and the digest's `Delta vs parent` block is computed against it.
+
+## Environment Variables
+
+| Variable | Purpose | Default |
+|---|---|---|
+| `HB_ROOT` | HANDBOOK.md checkout (tasks, `.env`) | required |
+| `HB_HARBOR` | Harbor executable with the benchmark's `agent_harness` installed | `$HB_ROOT/.venv/bin/harbor` |
+| `HARBOR_MODEL` | Worker model (`provider/model`) | `openrouter/qwen/qwen3.6-27b` |
+| `HB_OPENROUTER_PROVIDER` | Pin OpenRouter providers for the worker (`a,b`, no fallbacks) | OpenRouter routing |
+| `HARBOR_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | Wall-clock limit per Harbor job | `14400` |
+| `HB_LEAK_CORPUS` | Leak-audit corpus (or `--leak-corpus`) | code audit skipped |
+| `VITALS_PYTHON` | Python with agent-vitals installed | the loop's interpreter |
+| `VITALS_MH_REFERENCE_GGUF` | BF16 GGUF of the worker model, for replay | see agent-vitals |
+| `VITALS_MH_DETOK_GGUF` | Small same-vocabulary GGUF for CPU tokenization | see agent-vitals |
+| `VITALS_MH_HANDBOOK_TOOLS_JSON` | Cached OpenAI tool schemas; otherwise converted in `HANDBOOK_IMAGE` | see agent-vitals |
+| `HANDBOOK_IMAGE` | Image used to convert logged tool definitions | `handbook_base` |
+
+API keys for the worker go in `$HB_ROOT/.env` or this directory's `.env`.
+
+## Key Files
+
+- `meta_harness.py`: the loop; `--validate-agent agents.<name>:AgentHarness` runs candidate validation alone.
+- `handbook_runner.py`: the `HandbookRunner` base every candidate subclasses.
+- `candidate_agent.py`: Harbor agent that runs a candidate in place of the benchmark's runner.
+- `agents/baseline_openhands.py`: the benchmark's own prompt and loop, with its section declarations.
+- `scripts/run_eval.sh`: benchmarks one candidate on `train`, `holdout` or `smoke`.
+- `.claude/skills/meta-harness-handbook/SKILL.md`: proposer instructions.
+
+Outputs go to `jobs/<run>/` (Harbor jobs, one per candidate) and `logs/<run>/` (`frontier_val.json`, `evolution_summary.jsonl`, `pending_eval.json`, `claude_sessions/`, `reports/`, `vitals/`).
