+## Read-Map Feedback (agent-vitals)
+
+`--vitals` adds feedback from [agent-vitals](https://github.com/zwycl/agent-vitals): after each benchmark, a fixed panel of validation predictions per system and dataset is replayed through a local copy of the worker model, and the next proposer receives a per-section digest of how the worker read each prompt. The benchmark score remains the only objective. Without the flag the loop is unchanged.
+
+Install agent-vitals in any Python environment, then:
+
+```bash
+export VITALS_PYTHON=/path/to/agent-vitals-env/bin/python   # default: the interpreter running meta_harness.py
+export VITALS_MH_REFERENCE_GGUF=/path/to/worker-bf16.gguf     # GGUF of the --model weights; replay runs on the GPU
+export VITALS_LLAMA_LIB=/path/to/agent-vitals/vendor/llama.cpp/build/bin/libllama.so
+uv run python meta_harness.py --iterations 10 --run-name my-run --vitals
+```
+
+`$VITALS_PYTHON -m vitals.cli metaharness config` prints the paths agent-vitals resolves (including `VITALS_MH_DETOK_GGUF`, the small same-vocabulary model used for tokenization).
+
+With `--vitals`:
+
+- Inner loops run with `TC_REPLAY_CAPTURE=1`. Validation is evaluated one prediction at a time, and each `val.json` gains `predictions`: the prompt, the response, every LLM call with its reasoning, and the memory system's `prompt_sections()` declaration when it validates.
+- After the baselines and after every iteration's benchmark, the loop runs `vitals metaharness replay-inloop` (`--vitals-subsample` examples per system and dataset, default 12) and then `vitals metaharness digest`, passing each candidate's `base_system` as its parent. Failures are reported and the run continues.
+- Raw stores go to `logs/<run>/vitals/<system>--<dataset>/store`, digests to `vitals_digest.md` and `vitals_digest.parquet` next to each `val.json`, and per-iteration reports to `logs/<run>/reports/vitals_iteration_NN.md`. `--fresh` removes them.
+- The proposer's task prompt gains a "Worker read maps" section with these paths, the agent-vitals raw-data schema and loader, and how to use them.
+
+Digest rows are named by `MemorySystem.prompt_sections(input)`; `agents/no_memory.py` has an example. Prompts without a valid declaration are split structurally.
+
 ## Layout Notes
 
 - `agents/` contains the baselines and generated candidates.
